      "starterCode": "",
      "desc": "Given raw_ids = [3, 1, 3, 2, 1, 4], deduplicate the list while strictly preserving its original insertion order by converting to a dictionary via dict.fromkeys(raw_ids) and back to a list in dedup_ids. Store len(dedup_ids) in unique_count.",
      "prompt": "<strong>[Medium] Order-Preserving List Deduplication via dict.fromkeys()</strong><p>Given <code>raw_ids = [3, 1, 3, 2, 1, 4]</code>: Deduplicate while preserving first-seen order using <code>dedup_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(raw_ids))</code>. Assign its length to <code>unique_count</code>.</p>",
      "ref": "raw_ids = [3, 1, 3, 2, 1, 4]\ndedup_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(raw_ids))\nunique_count = len(dedup_ids)\nprint(f\"Dedup: {dedup_ids} | Count: {unique_count}\")\n",
      "solution": "raw_ids = [3, 1, 3, 2, 1, 4]\ndedup_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(raw_ids))\nunique_count = len(dedup_ids)\nprint(f\"Dedup: {dedup_ids} | Count: {unique_count}\")\n",
